{"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"CartesianProductView"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"First"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Second"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Vertices","type":"text"}]},{"text":" are the pairs ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Pair(g, h)"},{"text":". Vertex (g, h) has index ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"index(g)·|V(H)| + index(h)"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row-major, the numbering of NamedGraphs’ grids, so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertex(atIndex:)"},{"text":" costs one division and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexIndex(of:)"},{"text":" one lookup in each factor.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Rows","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" list the G-moves first, ","type":"text"},{"code":"(g′, h)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for each entry g′ of G’s row of g, then the H-moves","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"(g, h′)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". They are computed from the factors’ index rows and never hash. A factor’s self-loop","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"gives a product self-loop, listed twice in an undirected row as the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Graph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" law asks.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Edges"}]},{"text":" are named by the factor edge and the factor vertex that generate them:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".first(edge: e, vertexIndex: h)"},{"text":" is G’s edge ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"e"},{"text":" at H’s vertex index ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"h"},{"text":", and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".second(vertexIndex: g, edge: e)"},{"text":" is H’s edge ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"e"},{"text":" at G’s vertex index ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"text":" lists every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".first"},{"text":" edge, G-edge outer, then every ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".second"},{"text":" edge, G-vertex outer. When both factors have","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edge indices, so does the product: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"index(e)·|V(H)| + h"},{"text":", then ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"m_G·|V(H)| + g·m_H + index(e)"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Products of multigraphs and pseudographs are defined edge by edge, so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeCount"},{"text":", the rows and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the degrees always agree.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To materialize it, pass it to a representation’s initializer. Products are "},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when both"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"factors are."}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/graphproducts\/cartesianproductview"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/CartesianProductView","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/CartesianProductView\/DirectedEdges","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/CartesianProductView\/EdgeIndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/CartesianProductView\/EdgeRow","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/CartesianProductView\/IndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/CartesianProductView\/UndirectedEdges"],"generated":true},{"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/CartesianProductView\/first","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/CartesianProductView\/second"],"generated":true},{"title":"Enumerations","anchor":"Enumerations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/CartesianProductView\/Position"],"generated":true},{"title":"Default Implementations","anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/CartesianProductView\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/CartesianProductView\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/CartesianProductView\/Graph-Implementations"],"generated":true}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"title":"CartesianProductView","externalID":"s:13GraphProdu